# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAGStrike -- .gitignore
#
# The entries under "RAGStrike runtime data" are the ones that matter most.  scans.db holds RAW,
# UNREDACTED evidence, which by design may include real credentials and real personal data that a
# target disclosed during a scan.  Reports are redacted by default but still describe real weaknesses
# in a real system.  Neither belongs in version control, ever.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- RAGStrike runtime data (see the note above) ----
#
# Note the `dir/*` form rather than `dir/`. Git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so `data/` followed by `!data/README.md` silently drops the README. Excluding the
# directory's *contents* keeps the negations working.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/README.md
reports/*
!reports/.gitkeep
!reports/README.md
logs/*
!logs/README.md
!logs/application/
!logs/scans/
!logs/errors/
!logs/debug/
logs/*/*
!logs/*/.gitkeep
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# ---- Local attack packs -- a developer's own work, not the project's ----
packs/*
!packs/.gitkeep
!packs/README.md

# ---- Secrets ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# ---- Python ----
# Tool caches. These regenerate on the next run and are pure noise in a diff.
# `.import_linter_cache` was the one gap: import-linter writes it on every `lint-imports`,
# so a contributor who ran the architecture check saw it as an untracked directory.
.import_linter_cache/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib60/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# ---- Virtual environments ----
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/

# ---- Tooling caches ----
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# ---- Editors and local tool state ----
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
# per-machine tool permissions; contains absolute paths, not shareable
.claude/settings.local.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---- OS ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- Docs build ----
site/
docs/_build/

# ---- Streamlit ----
.streamlit/secrets.toml
